# Every path in this repo is owned by its subject.
#
# NOTE ON WHAT THIS CURRENTLY DOES: nothing, by necessity.
#
# The "main protection" ruleset sets require_code_owner_review = false. That is
# not an oversight — GitHub does not let you approve your own pull request, so
# on a single-maintainer repo any code-owner review requirement is an immediate
# and permanent lockout. The real gate is the required `scan` check, which no
# one can approve their way past.
#
# This file is therefore staged for a future that may not arrive: the moment a
# second person gets push access, flip require_code_owner_review to true and
# this starts enforcing. Kept deliberately so that decision is one setting
# rather than an archaeology exercise.

